  "Korean connectivity demand behaves the OPPOSITE way to Turkish, and the contrast is the most useful thing either measurement produced. In Turkish the eSIM intent is generic and the per-country phrasing tops out at 100. In Korean it is per-country and it carries the highest CPCs measured anywhere in this project: ilbon esim 2,400 at $0.30, miguk esim 600 at $0.60, yeongguk esim 200 at $0.70, dogil esim 150 at $0.70, itallia esim 150 at $0.60. So the destination half of the gate, which no Turkish country cleared easily, is cleared comfortably here by twelve countries.",
  "The domestic half is large and deep. Gyeongbokgung reads 22,000, Seoraksan 7,100, Namsan Tower 6,000, Hallasan 5,600, Hongdae 5,400, Seoul restaurants 3,700, Myeongdong 3,600, Seongsan Ilchulbong 3,500, Itaewon 3,100, Gwangalli 3,000, Bulguksa 2,900, Bukhansan 2,900. The city family reaches far down: Namwon 200 and Boryeong 60 are small cities with measured demand, the same shape the Turkish measurement found at Datca and Kas.",
  "Korea is NOT captured. It appears in neither the destination queue nor the market candidate queue, so none of that domestic demand is buildable today. This is the one candidate whose DESTINATION half is more buildable than its domestic half, because Japan is captured in full (31,095 rows today) and Japan is where Korean searchers overwhelmingly look: 44 of the measured keywords are about Japanese places and they carry 130,000 of the volume.",
  "Weather is the top Korean destination family and was REFUSED in Turkish. Tokyo weather reads 13,000 and Osaka weather 12,000 in Korean, against istanbul nisan ayi hava durumu at 70 in Turkish. Two markets admitted on the same day, one of them refusing the family the other leads with: that is what measuring per (family, market) rather than per family buys.",
  "Four countries with real travel volume are refused on the connectivity half: Netherlands (amseuteureudam yeohaeng 300 but neodeollandeu esim 10), Portugal (poreutugal yeohaeng 1,600 but esim 10), Czechia (peuraha yeohaeng 700 but esim 0) and Greece (geuriseu santorini 1,300 but esim 0). Portugal at 1,600 travel volume and 10 connectivity is the clearest case in either market of a country that wants reading about and does not want a SIM, which is exactly the asymmetry the two-half rule exists to catch."
 ],
 "serp_evidence": "NOT_SAMPLED_YET",
